EXT. CABLE CAR - ABOVE A GORGE - DUSK

A steel gondola dangles over a mile of nothing. Wind. Fog beneath. Six strangers are packed inside, breathing hard.

BRONWYN DAVIES, fifties, retired nurse. TEODORO "TEO" BIANCHI, twenties, backpacker. SAMIRA HADDAD, forties, mother, clutching a thermos. KWAME BOATENG, sixties, engineer, calm. ASTRID NYGAARD, thirties, runner. HIROSHI "HIRO" KAWAGUCHI, eighties, quiet, folded into the corner.

The car swings once. Settles.

KWAME
Everyone breathe. It's a power cut. The backup will come on.

SAMIRA
How long?

KWAME
Twenty minutes. Maybe thirty.

TEO
It's been forty.

KWAME
Then it's coming.

ASTRID
I run this gorge every Sunday. There's a ranger hut on the north side. If we climb out--

BRONWYN
We are not climbing out.

ASTRID
It's four hundred feet to the ridge.

BRONWYN
It's four hundred feet in the wrong direction.

HIRO
(softly)
Please. The car rocks.

SAMIRA
He's right. Nobody move.

TEO
I have a radio on my phone. No bars.

KWAME
Try the emergency channel.

TEO
It's not that kind of phone.

ASTRID
Then why do you have it?

TEO
For music.

BRONWYN
Lord.

SAMIRA
There is water in the thermos. Tea. We share.

KWAME
Small sips.

SAMIRA
Hiro, you first.

HIRO
Thank you.

BRONWYN
Hiro, how are you feeling?

HIRO
I am eighty-four. I have been in worse. In fifty-eight, I was in a cave for two days.

TEO
What happened?

HIRO
We sang.

ASTRID
Sang what?

HIRO
Whatever we knew. Bad songs. Many verses.

SAMIRA
(laughs)
Let's do that then.

KWAME
Singing in a swaying car is not--

BRONWYN
Kwame, let the man have his song.

KWAME
Fine. But quietly.

HIRO
I know one.

TEO
Go.

HIRO
(sings, thin)
"Hotaru no hikari..."

SAMIRA
I know this one! It's the school tune.

BRONWYN
Auld Lang Syne. We all know it.

ASTRID
(joining)
"Should auld acquaintance be forgot..."

TEO
I don't know the words.

KWAME
Hum.

All six now. Low. Wind carries them across the dark.

A groan from above. The cable shudders. Everyone stops.

ASTRID
Did that--

KWAME
Don't say it.

TEO
It's the wheel. It's coming back on.

BRONWYN
Or it's the other thing.

SAMIRA
What other thing?

KWAME
There's no other thing.

HIRO
There is always another thing.

The car lurches. A hiss, a clunk. The lights stutter on. Motor whirs.

TEO
YES!

ASTRID
Oh thank God.

SAMIRA
Hiro, you did it.

HIRO
The song did it.

The gondola begins to move. Slow. Steady. Toward the lit station.

BRONWYN
(low, to Kwame)
Funny. It's going the wrong way.

KWAME
(looking out)
That's not the station.

The lights ahead are a ranger hut. A single window. A figure with a rifle.

SAMIRA
Kwame?

KWAME
(quiet)
Nobody say anything.
